i3[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-i3/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Derive plurals and display aliases in the Rust glossary domain[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core: add phrase pluralization to sase-core, split authored / effective [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]/ display alias lists, and expose the new display list on the glossary [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Publish a sase-core-rs release containing the glossary change[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-release[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-release: land the release-plz version bump for sase-core and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]confirm the new sase-core-rs wheel resolves from PyPI.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Render display aliases and raise the core floor in sase[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]python[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-release[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]python: raise the sase-core-rs floor, carry the display alias list [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the Python facade and LSP payload, render it in generated [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glossary memory, and regenerate the agent instruction files.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-i3","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-i3.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-eb0f1669050dbce170e0a5b831103d99","started_at":"2026-08-09T12:20:10.736123+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable"